        "notes": [
          "Linked source occurrence is non-lyric performance material; lyric authorship is not applicable."
        ],
        "english_text": "(Saying so, they begin playing drums and pipes. They seat Uma and Sokkalingam on a plank and chant mantras..... They tie a groom’s turban on Sokkalingam’s head. They tie a small stone to a cord and tell him to fasten it around Uma’s neck. Just as he is about to tie the cord around Uma’s neck, the zamindar’s hand knocks his hand aside and snatches the cord away...)"
      }
